        "body": "Define how each Chat node records that its single conversation created, revised, explained, reviewed, or otherwise contributed to a graph or node. Support many Chat nodes across an artifact lifetime through ordinary graph relationships, without exposing commit history or reconstructing prior graph states.",
        "priority": "high",
        "status": "done",
        "owner": "Michael",
        "estimateHours": "2",
        "acceptanceCriteria": [
          "The v0.1 relationship vocabulary is small and semantically distinct.",
          "Produced-artifact references use durable graph or node addresses.",
          "The relationship remains understandable from either connected artifact.",
          "Each provenance relationship identifies the affected graph or node and the contribution role, without requiring a commit or historical snapshot.",
          "Several Chat nodes can independently contribute to the same graph without being merged into one conversation record.",
          "Event timestamps provide useful ordering without claiming to reconstruct a complete version history."
        ],
